## Dead Ends
An endpoint-wide strong cache map would violate router lifetime ownership. Looking up runtime metadata for every request would add unnecessary hot-path work. Prefix-monotonic stopping and rounding down a later hybrid hit are unsound for sliding-window or Mamba state. The implementation instead validates changed snapshots, traverses learned identities once, and proves each candidate endpoint. An early consumer compile command disabled required benchmark features; the corrected feature set passed.

