## Codebase Discoveries
Normalized GPU integer hashes expose only low 64 bits while store keys retain full SHA-256 digests. Useful supported geometry includes FA32 plus SWA8/window8, but not SWA8/window16. The final three-group TP2 debug benchmark averaged 8422.0 microseconds for 4096 blocks and 39280.4 microseconds for 16384 blocks over 32 runs each. Measured backing-map allocations at fixed caps were about 98.5 MiB live and 117 MiB during growth; these are not process RSS or total cache memory.

